WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.569
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.940
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.476
Well, guys, some big news
out of Washington today.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.711
House Democrats sent
former President Trump

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.880
a letter inviting him
to testify under oath

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.449
at his impeachment trial.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.151
There's no way
Trump's going to Washington.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.520
In fact, Trump's lawyers already
called this a publicity stunt,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.124
which backfired when Trump
was like, "Okay, now I'm in."

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:27.327
And get this --
after the Screen Actors Guild

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.961
criticized Trump last month,

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:31.764
today he sent a letter saying
that he's quitting the union.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.300
Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.302
Trump's out of work
and just quit his union.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.604
Even worse, now if he wants
medical coverage,

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.639
he's got to sign up
for Obamacare.

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:43.876
I mean, it just keeps --
It just keeps going.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:47.279
It's like, "Oh, my God."

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.515
Meanwhile, Melania heard
and was like, "Um, Donald,

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.817
while we're on the subject
of leaving unions..."

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.553
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.389
But check this out.
In the letter,

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.691
Trump actually bragged
about his acting credits.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.628
This is real. He wrote,
"I'm very proud of my work

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.230
on movies such as
'Home Alone 2,' 'Zoolander,'

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.998
and 'Wall Street:
Money Never Sleeps'

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:09.536
and television shows including
The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.'"

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.804
One day, you're the most
powerful man on Earth.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.040
The next, you're bragging
about your one line

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.742
in "Home Alone 2."

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.444
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.946
I forgot Trump
was on "Fresh Prince."

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.282
It turns out
he was the third Aunt Viv.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.883
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.753
Well, guys, the Super Bowl
is just a few days away,

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.622
but if you're thinking of
throwing a party on Sunday,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.292
you might want to listen to
what Dr. Fauci has to say.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.959 line:0%
-Absolutely not.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:37.096 line:0%
I mean, watch the Super Bowl
on TV, enjoy it,

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.832 line:0%
have a party in your house
with your family.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:43.669 line:0%
So, as difficult as that is,
at least this time around,

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.738 line:0%
just lay low and cool it.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.873
-Fauci was like,
"This is about public health

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.808
and definitely not
because it's Thursday

00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:51.510
and I still haven't
been invited to one.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.879
Just want to make that clear.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.815
But had I been or have I been,
I would not go.

00:01:56.815 --> 00:02:00.052
Of course not."

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.055
Listen to this, guys.
I read that if the Buccaneers

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.823 line:0%
win on Sunday,
Tom Brady will get

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.359 line:0%
a $500,000 bonus.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.428 line:0%
When he heard that,
Brady was like, "Golly.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.630
I better start practicing."

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.499
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.135
It's a $500,000 "incentive."

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.137
I don't even understand
why they do this.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.406
Who needs an incentive
to try and win the Super Bowl?

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.576
It's like,
"All right. Now I'll try."

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.811
When asked why he had that
added to his contract,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.312
Brady said...

00:02:27.312 --> 00:02:29.115
"Because it's funny."

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.284
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.355
Get this. Down in Tampa,
the local news decided

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.657
to talk to a 99-year-old
Buccaneers fan.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.660
She's pretty fired up
about the game. Watch this.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.962
-The Bucs
is the ones that I love.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.965
Tom Brady. We did it.
We kicked [bleep].

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:50.903
Now Patrick is coming to our
house to get his [bleep] kicked.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:54.340
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.809
The news anchor was like,
"Wow. I did not think

00:02:56.809 --> 00:03:00.613
that we needed the bleep button
for that segment, but, okay."

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.914
Yeah, she and Tom go way back.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.816
She was actually
a Patriots cheerleader

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.885
during his rookie season.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.953
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.923
Yeah, she's the only fan
of the Buccaneers

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:13.459
who knew actual buccaneers.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.361
This is interesting.
I heard that each year

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.996
a handful of
Super Bowl commercials

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.498
are rejected by TV networks.
Either they're too controversial

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:21.334
or just not right
for the big game.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.202
We got our hands on one of them,
and you can see

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.437
why it didn't make it, I think.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.171
Take a look.

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:30.609
-Clydesdales. Powerful. Mighty.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.345
And now available

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.714
in every scoop of tuna
at Subway.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.415
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:39.218
-That is awful. That is awful.
That is terr-- That is --

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.520
That should not --
That should not air.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.556
That should not air
on television.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.325
I agree. Good for them.
That's terrible.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.294
-Oh, my God.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.229
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.231
-Check this out.
In Saudi Arabia,

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.867
there's a roller coaster
that's opening in 2023

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.170
that will travel more than
155 miles per hour.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.272
And they released
a simulation video.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:01.941
This is real. Watch this.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.809
[ Riders screaming ]

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:09.449
♪♪

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.017
You know it's an insane idea
when even the simulated people

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.553
are screaming.

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:14.987
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.990
Listen to this.
I read about a man in Florida

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.758
who was caught trying
to board a flight

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:22.395
with 22 pounds of meth
in his luggage.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.830
Yeah, luggage with
22 pounds of meth,

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.799
or, as it's known
in Florida, luggage.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.067
There you go.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:31.203
[ Applause ]
Thank you.

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:33.906
And, finally, as I said before,
the Super Bowl is this Sunday

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.842
with the Kansas City Chiefs
taking on the Tampa Bay
Buccaneers.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:38.444
Now, as you know,
after the game,

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.413
they give out awards like
Most Valuable Player,

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.348
but they also give out awards
before the game.

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.649
I'll show you what I mean.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.285
It's time for
"Tonight Show Superlatives."

